{"id": "e83a4952-981f-4bb0-8e58-5c2ca915b050", "title": {"en": "Shakey Energy", "es": "Energ\u00eda Agitada", "pt": "Energia Agitada"}, "card": {"foregroundColor": {"blue": 1, "green": 1, "opacity": 1, "red": 1}, "image": "", "imageStyle": "textFirst", "localizedTitle": {"en": "### Shakey Energy", "es": "### Energ\u00eda Agitada", "pt": "### Energia Vibrante"}}, "pages": [{"id": "a7c8fb77-5d1e-45f8-91d3-9f43fde1e982", "blocks": [{"id": "8cfbbe71-c749-478a-95e9-729c36e11b44", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Did you know human activity can cause an Earthquake?", "es": "## \u00bfSab\u00edas que la actividad humana puede causar terremotos?", "pt": "## Voc\u00ea sabia que a atividade humana pode causar terremotos?"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "633310cb-a233-412f-823f-24a38d0d0507", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Usually these are very minor earthquakes (Magnitude 2 or less) and are\ncaused by minor stresses and strains put on the Earth by things like fossil-fuel\nextraction, geothermal energy operations, and injection of waste water from\nhydraulic fracturing.\n\nThese types of Earthquakes are called **Induced Earthquakes** and are often too \nsmall to be felt by humans at the surface of the Earth.\n\nHowever, occasionally these activities lead to larger earthquakes with a \nmagnitude 4+.\n", "es": "Por lo general, son terremotos muy d\u00e9biles (magnitud 2 o inferior) y son\ncausados por tensiones menores aplicadas a la Tierra por actividades tales\ncomo la extracci\u00f3n de combustibles f\u00f3siles, operaciones de energ\u00eda geot\u00e9rmica\no la inyecci\u00f3n de aguas residuales del *fracking* hidr\u00e1ulico.\n\nEstos tipos de terremotos se denominan **terremotos inducidos** y, a menudo,\nson demasiado d\u00e9biles como para que los humanos los sientan en la superficie\nde la Tierra.\n\nSin embargo, ocasionalmente estas actividades producen terremotos m\u00e1s fuerte\ncon una magnitud de 4 o m\u00e1s.\n", "pt": "Geralmente, esses s\u00e3o terremotos muito pequenos (magnitude 2 ou menos) e s\u00e3o \ncausados por tens\u00f5es e press\u00f5es menores exercidas sobre a Terra por atividades\ncomo extra\u00e7\u00e3o de combust\u00edveis f\u00f3sseis, opera\u00e7\u00f5es de energia geot\u00e9rmica e inje\u00e7\u00e3o\nde \u00e1gua residual proveniente do fraturamento hidr\u00e1ulico.\n\nEsse tipo de terremoto \u00e9 chamado de terremoto induzido e, muitas vezes, \u00e9 pequeno \ndemais para ser sentido pelas pessoas na superf\u00edcie da Terra.\n\nNo entanto, ocasionalmente essas atividades podem levar a terremotos maiores, \ncom magnitude superior a 4.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "7b63377d-5b8b-4972-8119-708f729f8349", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}], "title": "P1. Induced Earthquakes"}, {"id": "da9e24ff-58fd-469e-a384-0a7526af9d38", "blocks": [{"id": "f960e3dc-45db-428d-9bbb-fadcba51eb9a", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Geothermal Energy", "es": "## Energ\u00eda geotermal", "pt": "## Energia Geot\u00e9rmica"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "26888c63-1d30-4f80-b15c-e5d28f9acb51", "height": "huge", "image": "", "type": "image"}, {"id": "14e9c400-8e7b-4ecd-99db-fa5b721d143e", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "In this example, we are going to look at a magnitude 5 earthquake caused\nby human activity at **The Geysers Geothermal Field** located in Northern\nCalifornia.\n", "es": "En este ejemplo, vamos a ver un terremoto de magnitud 5 causado por la actividad\nhumana en **The Geysers Geothermal Field** ubicado en el norte de California.\n", "pt": "Neste exemplo, vamos observar um terremoto de magnitude 5 causado pela atividade\nhumana no **Geysers Geothermal Field**, localizado no norte da Calif\u00f3rnia.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "7d4023a5-39a7-4da2-8836-0748bf3d5cc2", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "There are 18 major geothermal plants in *The Geysers Geothermal Field* making\nit the largest system of Geothermal Plants in the world.\n\nSeismologists believe there may be several sources for the seismic activity\nin this area including the injection of water into the bedrock, and the extraction\nof steam causing the surrounding bedrock to contract.\n", "es": "Hay 18 importantes plantas geot\u00e9rmicas en *The Geysers Geothermal Field*,\nlo que las convierte en el sistema de plantas geot\u00e9rmicas m\u00e1s grande del mundo.\n\nLos sism\u00f3logos creen que puede haber varias fuentes para la actividad s\u00edsmica\nen este \u00e1rea, como la inyecci\u00f3n de agua en el lecho rocoso o la extracci\u00f3n\nde vapor que hace que el lecho rocoso circundante se contraiga.\n", "pt": "Existem 18 plantas geot\u00e9rmicas importantes no **Geysers Geothermal Field**,\nfazendo com que esse seja o maior sistema de plantas geotermais do mundo.\n\nOs sism\u00f3logos acreditan que possam haver v\u00e1rias causas para a atividade s\u00edsmica\nnesta \u00e1rea, como a inje\u00e7\u00e3o de \u00e1gua no leito rochoso, e a extra\u00e7\u00e3o de vapor, que\nfaz com que o leito rochoso ao redor se contraia.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "da5c7ccf-d0da-4c1c-a3d5-a5b78ee90e3f", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Take a moment to listen to this induced earthquake:", "es": "Escucha este terremoto inducido:", "pt": "Escute esse terremoto induzido:"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "fe5b0807-0747-4e77-8c8f-7e6258ed5da3", "octavesHigher": 512, "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 9000, "startDate": "2016-12-14T16:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "user", "id": "4DEE77F4-3827-4DA1-83AF-E522FA2A91A5", "name": "California", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "location": "00", "network": "BK", "station": "MCCM"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 0}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "9947f3d2-e822-4f11-96ed-c3800f9463af", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "> **Note:** The earthquake occurred on December 14, 2016, and the recording of its seismic waves was made 80 km from the epicenter.", "es": "> **Nota:** el terremoto ocurri\u00f3 el 14 de Diciembre de 2016 y su onda s\u00edsmica se registr\u00f3 a 80 km del epicentro.", "pt": "> **Nota:** O terremoto ocorreu em 14 de dezembro de 2016 e sua onda s\u00edsmica foi registradas a 80 km do epicentro."}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "aeb993b8-c3f8-4f87-b9a8-5ca237060484", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Now compare it to another earthquake of similar magnitude (M5) that occurred naturally via plate tectonics.", "es": "Ahora comp\u00e1ralo con otro terremoto con magnitud similar (M5) que ocurri\u00f3 de forma natural via placas tect\u00f3nicas.", "pt": "Agora compare este evento com um terremoto de magnitude similar (M5) que ocorreu de forma natural via placas tect\u00f4nicas."}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "e8ebb38e-5427-4941-aaf1-11361eb3d77b", "octavesHigher": 512, "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 7200, "startDate": "2009-03-24T11:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "user", "id": "808CDF29-ADDC-4D70-9DFD-0A084B00B24A", "name": "California", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "location": "00", "network": "II", "station": "PFO"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 0}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "87ccf293-9182-464d-8030-c49d462a7dea", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "> **Note:** This earthquake occurred on March 24, 2009, and the recording of its seismic waves was made 80 km from the epicenter.", "es": "> **Nota:** el terremoto ocurri\u00f3 el 24 de Marzo de 2009 y la onda s\u00edsmica se registro a 80 km del epicentro.", "pt": "> **Nota:** O terremoto ocorreu em 24 de Mar\u00e7o de 2009 e a onda s\u00edsmica foi registrada a 80 km do epicentro."}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "b4b7ac22-cc98-40de-9341-bd573c8cac7e", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Questions", "es": "## Preguntas", "pt": "## Perguntas"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "eef4532d-7121-4c4b-bfbd-db82a70cce07", "backgroundTransparent": false, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 1.** How do these earthquakes of similar magnitude and recording distance compare?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 1.** \u00bfC\u00f3mo comparar\u00edas estos terremotos similares en magnitud y distancia de\nregistro?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 1.** Como estes terremotos de magnitude e dist\u00e2ncia de registro similares se \ncomparam um ao outro?\n"}}, {"id": "c7ca12fe-ddbd-4595-9574-f8cae3676a6a", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "They look and sound similar, but not exactly the same. Few earthquake signals \nlook and sound exactly like another.\n", "es": "Se ven y suenan similares, pero no exactamente iguales. Pocas se\u00f1ales de terremotos \nse ven y suenan exactamente como otras.\n", "pt": "Eles t\u00eam apar\u00eancia e som semelhantes, mas n\u00e3o exatamente iguais. Poucos sinais de\nterremotos ser\u00e3o exatamente iguais em apar\u00eancia e sonoridade.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Revelar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "565b6818-6294-4770-b36e-5c8c9a8c8cd6", "backgroundTransparent": false, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 2.** Do you notice any major differences between the induced earthquake vs.\nthe naturally occurring earthquake?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 2.** \u00bfNotas alguna diferencia importante entre el terremoto inducido y el terremoto\nque ocurre naturalmente?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 2.** Voc\u00ea nota alguma diferen\u00e7a importante entre o terremoto induzido e o terremoto\nque ocorre naturalmente?\n"}}, {"id": "4dc82c83-e84f-4949-aab9-050675ef9ba8", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "The tectonic (natural) earthquake seems to be followed by weaker-sounding aftershocks.\n", "es": "El terremoto tect\u00f3nico (natural) parece ser seguido por r\u00e9plicas de sonido m\u00e1s d\u00e9bil.\n", "pt": "O terremoto tect\u00f4nico (natural) parece ser seguido por r\u00e9plicas de som mais fraco.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Revelar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "3bf61316-5819-492d-8174-616904d45159", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}, {"id": "1f3ac1a4-b9cc-48ba-ad3e-6f6d134ccd2c", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "Image credit: ***Shaul Hurwitz, USGS. Public domain.***", "es": "Cr\u00e9ditos de la imagen: ***Shaul Hurwitz, USGS. Public domain.***", "pt": "Cr\u00e9ditos da imagem: ***Shaul Hurwitz, USGS. Public domain.***"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}], "title": "P2. Geothermal Energy"}, {"id": "15d49066-9144-4f94-ae74-af6a257c51a8", "blocks": [{"id": "160865be-9a62-47f9-a58e-6c0849b42f34", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Wastewater from Oil and Gas Drilling", "es": "## Aguas residuales de perforaciones de petr\u00f3leo y gas", "pt": "## \u00c1guas residuais de perfura\u00e7\u00f5es de petr\u00f3leo e g\u00e1s"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "3ff98b70-987b-4a5c-9606-c76c48a85770", "height": "regular", "image": "", "type": "image"}, {"id": "955c1c22-262f-4b5d-a90e-5d4f16cc486f", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "In September of 2016, the town of Pawnee, Oklahoma, had its largest earthquake\nsince the 1950s at a Magnitude of 5.8.\n\nOklahoma is naturally a slightly seismically active region of the United States \n(a magnitude 5 or greater earthquake every 500 years), as it contains a series \nof fault systems.\n\nHowever, scientists have noticed the intensity and **occurrence of seismic\nactivity has increased** in recent years correlating to an increase of wastewater\ninjection practices associated with unconventional oil extraction processes.\n", "es": "En septiembre de 2016, la ciudad de Pawnee, Oklahoma, tuvo su mayor terremoto\ndesde la d\u00e9cada de 1950 con una magnitud de 5,8.\n\nOklahoma es una regi\u00f3n de Estados Unidos con una leve actividad s\u00edsmica natural \n(un terremoto de magnitud 5 o mayor cada 500 a\u00f1os), ya que contiene una serie de \nsistemas de fallas.\n\nSin embargo, los cient\u00edficos han notado que la intensidad y **la frecuencia de \nla actividad s\u00edsmica ha aumentado** en los \u00faltimos a\u00f1os en correlaci\u00f3n con un \naumento de las pr\u00e1cticas de inyecci\u00f3n de aguas residuales asociadas con los \nprocesos de extracci\u00f3n de petr\u00f3leo no convencionales.\n", "pt": "Em setembro de 2016, a cidade de Pawnee, Oklahoma, registrou seu maior terremoto \ndesde a d\u00e9cada de 1950, com uma magnitude de 5.8.\n\nOklahoma \u00e9, naturalmente, uma regi\u00e3o ligeiramente sismicamente ativa dos Estados Unidos\n(um terremoto de magnitude 5 ou maior a cada 500 anos), pois cont\u00e9m uma s\u00e9rie de sistemas\nde falhas.\n\nNo entanto, os cientistas notaram que a intensidade e a ocorr\u00eancia da atividade \ns\u00edsmica aumentaram nos \u00faltimos anos, correlacionando-se com o aumento das pr\u00e1ticas\nde inje\u00e7\u00e3o de \u00e1gua residual associadas aos processos n\u00e3o convencionais de extra\u00e7\u00e3o \nde petr\u00f3leo.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "1394092a-decc-4986-adc5-8ea90a68eb8d", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Listen to the audio file of seismic waves from this earthquake as monitored by a seismic station in Illinois, about 1000 km away from Pawnee, Oklahoma.", "es": "Escucha la siguiente onda s\u00edsmica de un terremoto monitoreado por una estaci\u00f3n s\u00edsmica en Illinois, a unos 1000 km de Pawnee, Oklahoma.", "pt": "Ou\u00e7a o arquivo de \u00e1udio das ondas s\u00edsmicas desse terremoto, registradas por uma esta\u00e7\u00e3o s\u00edsmica em Illinois, a cerca de 1000 km de dist\u00e2ncia de Pawnee, Oklahoma."}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "85d062eb-bca4-404a-963c-dbd46c148e02", "type": "localWave", "waveData": {"duration": 3600, "startDate": "2016-09-03T12:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "example", "id": "3CCF5D30-6F15-4D16-98AC-7F02934AFDDE", "latitude": 39.72, "longitude": -91.51, "name": "Illinois", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "from": "2011-10-10T00:00:00Z", "location": "--", "network": "TA", "station": "L44A", "to": "2015-10-16T18:00:00Z"}, {"channel": "HHZ", "from": "2015-10-16T18:00:00Z", "location": "--", "network": "TA", "station": "L44A", "to": "2019-03-14T19:55:00Z"}, {"channel": "HHZ", "from": "2019-03-15T01:09:00Z", "location": "00", "network": "NW", "station": "L44A"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "America/Chicago", "style": "byName"}, "timeLatency": 24}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "89098194-5427-4175-84d0-2ba24d27e9a3", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "> **Note:** This earthquake occurred on September 3, 2016, and the recording of its seismic waves was made 1000 km to the north-east of the epicenter, in Illinois.", "es": "> **Nota:** el terremoto ocurri\u00f3 el 3 de Septiembre de 2016 y la onda s\u00edsmica se registr\u00f3 a 1000 km al noreste del epicentro, en Illinois.", "pt": "> **Nota:** O terremoto aconteceu em 3 de setembro de 2016 e a onda s\u00edsmica foi registrada a 1000 km noroeste do epicentro, em Illinois."}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "14253ce4-6010-4707-8e79-8db9a6127319", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Question", "es": "## Pregunta", "pt": "## Pergunta"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "88b77d61-8a8f-4110-857b-c9eaf85171b6", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 1.** Do you think this earthquake in Pawnee, Oklahoma, would have occurred if\nthe practice of waste water injection didn\u2019t exist in this area? If no, why\nnot? If yes, would it have occurred at the same time or one, ten, hundred,\nor a thousand years later?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 1.** \u00bfCrees que el terremoto de Pawnee, Oklahoma, hubiese ocurrido si la pr\u00e1ctica\nde la inyecci\u00f3n de aguas residuales no existiera en esta \u00e1rea? En caso negativo,\n\u00bfpor qu\u00e9 no? En caso afirmativo, \u00bfhubiese ocurrido al mismo tiempo o uno,\ndiez, cien o mil a\u00f1os despu\u00e9s?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 1.** Voc\u00ea acha que esse terremoto em Pawnee, Oklahoma, teria ocorrido se a pr\u00e1tica \nde inje\u00e7\u00e3o de \u00e1gua residual n\u00e3o existisse nessa regi\u00e3o? Se n\u00e3o, por qu\u00ea? \nSe sim, ele teria ocorrido no mesmo momento ou daqui a um, \ndez, cem ou mil anos?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "54b1a399-5dc9-4671-85e4-4479bd4a7959", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "There is no unique answer; this is about what you think. If you think **no** you might say so \nbecause Oklahoma typically experiences very low seismic activity and this earthquake occurred \nduring a period of significant wastewater injection and significantly increased seismic activity. \n\nIf you think **yes** you might say so because intraplate earthquakes do occasionally occur in \nNorth America and other continents and this could be one of them. Without waste-water injection \npotentially facilitating the release of intraplate stress, this earthquake might have occurred \nhundreds to thousands of years later than it did.\n", "es": "No hay una respuesta \u00fanica; depende de lo que pienses. Si piensas que **no**, podr\u00edas decirlo \nporque Oklahoma normalmente experimenta una actividad s\u00edsmica muy baja y este terremoto ocurri\u00f3 \ndurante un per\u00edodo de inyecci\u00f3n significativa de aguas residuales y un aumento considerable de \nla actividad s\u00edsmica.\n\nSi piensas que **s\u00ed**, podr\u00edas decirlo porque los terremotos intraplaca ocasionalmente ocurren \nen Am\u00e9rica del Norte y otros continentes, y este podr\u00eda ser uno de ellos. Sin la inyecci\u00f3n de \naguas residuales potencialmente facilitando la liberaci\u00f3n del estr\u00e9s intraplaca, este terremoto \npodr\u00eda haber ocurrido cientos o miles de a\u00f1os m\u00e1s tarde de cuando ocurri\u00f3.\n", "pt": "N\u00e3o existe uma resposta \u00fanica \u2014 trata-se do que voc\u00ea pensa. Se voc\u00ea acha que a resposta \u00e9 **n\u00e3o**, \npode justificar dizendo que Oklahoma normalmente apresenta uma atividade s\u00edsmica muito baixa, \ne esse terremoto ocorreu durante um per\u00edodo de inje\u00e7\u00e3o significativa de \u00e1gua residual e aumento\nnot\u00e1vel da atividade s\u00edsmica.\n\nSe voc\u00ea acha que a resposta \u00e9 **sim**, pode argumentar que terremotos intraplaca ocasionalmente \nocorrem na Am\u00e9rica do Norte e em outros continentes, e que esse poderia ser um deles. Sem a inje\u00e7\u00e3o de          \u00e1gua residual potencialmente facilitando a libera\u00e7\u00e3o do estresse intraplaca, esse terremoto poderia ter         acontecido centenas ou at\u00e9 milhares de anos depois do que aconteceu.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Revelar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "86c7e406-d3b2-4ba6-be62-615a2c293c25", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}, {"id": "b214d34e-2dd6-4512-b286-ef316ab984c4", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "Image credit: ***https://pxhere.com/en/photo/775734***", "es": "Cr\u00e9ditos de la imagen: ***https://pxhere.com/en/photo/775734***", "pt": "Cr\u00e9ditos da imagem: ***https://pxhere.com/en/photo/775734***"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}], "title": "P3. Wastewater from oil and gas drilling"}, {"id": "09f3fee2-d269-43fd-8b9a-219a1dbd199c", "blocks": [{"id": "8a6479a0-87e7-44de-8df8-22c156df9ac4", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Wastewater from Oil and Gas Drilling (II)", "es": "## Aguas residuales de perforaciones de petr\u00f3leo y gas (II)", "pt": "## \u00c1guas Residuais de Perfura\u00e7\u00f5es de Petr\u00f3leo e G\u00e1s (II)"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "f084fa25-f257-4250-ae52-526defcfe4f3", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Seismic waves that propagated from Oklahoma to Illinois traveled through\nthe rigid continental interior of the North-American plate. Seismic waves\nthat propagate from Oklahoma to the west enter into deformed and less rigid,\nmore ductile crust of the North American plate.\n", "es": "Las ondas s\u00edsmicas que se propagaron desde Oklahoma a Illinois viajaron\na trav\u00e9s del interior r\u00edgido de la placa continental Norteamericana. Las ondas\ns\u00edsmicas que se propagan desde Oklahoma hacia el oeste entran en la corteza\ndeformada de la placa Norteamericana, menos r\u00edgida y m\u00e1s d\u00factil.\n", "pt": "As ondas s\u00edsmicas que se propagaram de Oklahoma at\u00e9 Illinois viajaram atrav\u00e9s do \ninterior continental r\u00edgido da placa Norte-Americana. J\u00e1 as ondas s\u00edsmicas que se \npropagam de Oklahoma para o oeste entram em uma crosta deformada e menos r\u00edgida, \nmais d\u00factil, da placa Norte-Americana.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "2cf33e74-bcac-4212-a982-88551edde9f3", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "This is the previous recording of the Pawnee Earthquake in Illinois:", "es": "Esta es la grabaci\u00f3n anterior del terremoto de Pawnee en Illinois:", "pt": "Esta \u00e9 a grava\u00e7\u00e3o anterior do terremoto de Pawnee em Illinois:"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "68784b11-47b6-492f-862a-f2474f8088c1", "type": "localWave", "waveData": {"duration": 3600, "startDate": "2016-09-03T12:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "example", "id": "3CCF5D30-6F15-4D16-98AC-7F02934AFDDE", "latitude": 39.72, "longitude": -91.51, "name": "Illinois", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "from": "2011-10-10T00:00:00Z", "location": "--", "network": "TA", "station": "L44A", "to": "2015-10-16T18:00:00Z"}, {"channel": "HHZ", "from": "2015-10-16T18:00:00Z", "location": "--", "network": "TA", "station": "L44A", "to": "2019-03-14T19:55:00Z"}, {"channel": "HHZ", "from": "2019-03-15T01:09:00Z", "location": "00", "network": "NW", "station": "L44A"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "America/Chicago", "style": "byName"}, "timeLatency": 24}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "cbf45701-54fd-44fc-9552-a44dbabb0b1b", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Let's compare it with another one made at a similar distance in the opposite\ndirection from the epicenter (New Mexico).\n", "es": "Compar\u00e9mosla con otra realizada a una distancia similar en la direcci\u00f3n\nopuesta al epicentro (Nuevo M\u00e9xico).\n", "pt": "Vamos compar\u00e1-lo com outro registro feito a uma dist\u00e2ncia semelhante, mas na \ndire\u00e7\u00e3o oposta a partir do epicentro (Novo M\u00e9xico). \n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "3d3198d2-3a4e-4cbc-b104-4cbede86da0f", "type": "localWave", "waveData": {"duration": 3600, "startDate": "2016-09-03T12:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "user", "id": "110DE775-1D07-4D9A-B215-BF69F3DCCB97", "name": "Mexico", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "location": "--", "network": "TA", "station": "Y22D"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 0}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "99d838b0-799f-4a1d-a346-04d9d76931c5", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "> **Note:** The M5.8 Pawnee, Oklahoma earthquake occurred on September 3, 2016, and the recording of its seismic waves was made 1000 km to the west and a little bit to the south of the epicenter, in New Mexico.", "es": "> **Nota:** El terremoto M5.8 de Pawnee, Oklahoma ocurri\u00f3 el 3 de Septiembre de 2016 y se registr\u00f3 a 1000 km al oeste y un poco al sur del epicentro, en Nuevo M\u00e9xico.", "pt": "> **Nota:** O terremoto de M5.8 de Pawnee, Oklahoma ocorreu em 3 de Setembro de 2016 e o registro de suas ondas s\u00edsmicas foi feito 1000 km ao oeste e um pouco ao sul do epicentro, no Novo M\u00e9xico."}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "246b1f4e-6415-49eb-b35a-7e0b2662e43f", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Compressed rocks deep in the Earth's crust near plate boundaries tends to\nbe more ductile in comparison to such rocks inside a stable part of a tectonic\nplate, which are more rigid.\n", "es": "Las rocas comprimidas en las profundidades de la corteza terrestre, cerca\nde los l\u00edmites de las placas, tienden a ser m\u00e1s d\u00factiles en comparaci\u00f3n con\nlas rocas que se encuentran dentro de la parte estable de la placa tect\u00f3nica,\nque son m\u00e1s r\u00edgidas.\n", "pt": "Rochas comprimidas nas profundezas da crosta terrestre, pr\u00f3ximas \u00e0s bordas das \nplacas tect\u00f4nicas, tendem a ser mais d\u00facteis em compara\u00e7\u00e3o com rochas semelhantes \nlocalizadas em partes est\u00e1veis de uma placa tect\u00f4nica, que s\u00e3o mais r\u00edgidas.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "97b4daa2-1d16-4e8f-979b-7cc84a6429bc", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Questions", "es": "## Preguntas", "pt": "## Perguntas"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "47786551-1458-4924-a2bd-7ff568448d4e", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 1.** Which one of these events corresponds to a higher pitch?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 1.** \u00bfCu\u00e1l de estos eventos tiene un tono m\u00e1s alto?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 1.** Qual destes eventos tem uma sonoridade (tom) mais aguda?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "c25098e6-4fc0-40b2-9a71-760133398df7", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "The one recorded in Illinois has a higher pitch. It's easier to hear with \nauto-adjusted volume.\n", "es": "El registrado en Illinois tiene un tono m\u00e1s alto. Es m\u00e1s f\u00e1cil de escuchar \ncon el volumen auto-ajustado.\n", "pt": "O evento registrado em Illinois tem a sonoridade (tom) mais aguda. \u00c9 mais f\u00e1cil\nescutar com o volume auto-ajustado.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Revelar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "3ff8c0ef-3781-4517-9845-4bc6697323cf", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 2.** What can you infer about the correlation between the rigidity of rock and\nthe pitch of these waves?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 2.** \u00bfQu\u00e9 puedes inferir acerca de la correlaci\u00f3n entre la rigidez de la roca\ny el tono de las ondas?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 2.** O que voc\u00ea pode inferir sobre a correla\u00e7\u00e3o entre a rigidez das rochas e o                       tom (frequ\u00eancia) dessas ondas?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "93cd6279-2fdf-490a-ba7d-b1fe56a15f63", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "New Mexico is west of the Rocky Mountains, which is a geologically active region above \na deforming crust and mantle. Illinois is east of the Rocky Mountains and its deep crust \nand mantle is more rigid and has not deformed for hundreds of millions of years.\n\nIt appears that the increased rigidity of the deep crust and mantle allows higher-pitched \nseismic waves to propagate over larger distances.\n", "es": "Nuevo M\u00e9xico est\u00e1 al oeste de las Monta\u00f1as Rocosas, una regi\u00f3n geol\u00f3gicamente activa \nsobre una corteza y manto en deformaci\u00f3n. Illinois est\u00e1 al este de las Monta\u00f1as Rocosas \ny su corteza profunda y manto son m\u00e1s r\u00edgidos y no se han deformado durante cientos de \nmillones de a\u00f1os. \n\nParece que el aumento de la rigidez de la corteza y el manto profundos permite que las \nondas s\u00edsmicas de tono m\u00e1s alto se propaguen a mayores distancias.\n", "pt": "O estado do Novo M\u00e9xico est\u00e1 a oeste das Montanhas Rochosas, que \u00e9 uma regi\u00e3o geologicamente \nativa acima de uma crosta e manto em deforma\u00e7\u00e3o. Illinois est\u00e1 a leste das Montanhas Rochosas, \ne sua crosta profunda e manto s\u00e3o mais r\u00edgidos e n\u00e3o sofreram deforma\u00e7\u00f5es por centenas de \nmilh\u00f5es de anos.\n\nParece que o aumento da rigidez da crosta e do manto profundos permite que ondas s\u00edsmicas \nde tom mais agudo se propaguem por dist\u00e2ncias maiores.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Revelar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "c48c6377-094c-48b9-8fd1-6812fc806201", "action": "close", "localizedText": {"en": "Close", "es": "Cerrar", "pt": "Fechar"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}], "title": "P4. More Wastewater from oil and gas drilling"}]}